window.products.push({"id":306377,"name":"Burlapper Burlap (14 Inch x 10 Yards, Natural)","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":19.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81ZPDdMBojL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"We're glad you stopped by to check out our 14 inch x 10 yard Burlapper burlap roll! We'd like to tell you a little about our burlap and why we think it's the best fabric available anywhere. Burlapper burlap is sourced directly from India. It is processed and custom cut to our specifications at a U.S.-based family operated mill that has been manufacturing burlap for over 100 years. Having access to over 5 million feet of burlap inventory allows us to handpick the best quality burlap fabric available. Once we choose our fabric, burlapper burlap is custom fabricated and cut to our exacting specifications. We then inspect and hand pack each piece of burlap before we ship it. This means that only the best quality burlap makes it to you, which is why every purchase is backed by a no questions asked, 100% money back guarantee! Whether you need one or 100 pieces of burlap, insist on genuine burlapperTM brand burlap by Sourcedly for the best quality, value, and selection. You'll find that the distinct characteristics of Burlapper 10 ounce, heavy weight burlap fabric make each piece unique. Burlap fabric is best known for its use as bagging, wrapping and in furniture manufacturing, but it has been popularized for hundreds of other uses. The simple elegance of our heavy, 10 oz., plain-woven Burlapper burlap fabric makes it ideally suited for table runners; arts, crafts and sewing projects; rustic weddings, landscaping, interior decorating, banners and signage, school projects, and much more. Burlap is also known by the names gunny and hessian. BURLAPPER SPECIFICATIONS: 14 inches wide x 10 yards long (30 feet / 360 inches). This 14\" wide burlap roll was cut to size by industrial slitters at the mill, which guarantees the straightest edge possible. Our 14\" rolls are free of colored marker lines that commonly run down one edge of the burlap. Both edges are unfinished and can be left as-is, serged, or sewn. Color: Natural, Grade A. Photos by: Sourcedly","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81ZPDdMBojL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Burlapper","source_asin":"B013X6QA38","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-306377","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B013X6QA38","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B013X6QA38","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
